That is quite unusual, because most of the early means of teleport would let 
you get out of the shop again. As you said, you could have re-read the 
cursed spellbook.

In the early game (especially if you don't care if you die), you might be 
able find several ways to escape a shop and steal everything that was in it. 
Even if you just do a simple teleport, Keystone Kops are easy to kill (and 
rewarding, in experience terms!) and they can often block the shopkeeper 
from reaching you too quickly. Also, ring shops are probably the most 
"valuable" shops in terms of what you can steal and what those items are 
worth, shop-wise -- rings and gems tend to be pricey -- so they're fun to 
rob.

I am really obsessed with shops. If I get to Minetown with a wand of death 
